        {
          "question": "e-4726",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Remember that an elementary matrix is obtained by performing exactly one elementary row operation on the identity matrix $I.$\n\nThe given matrix $E$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from $I$ by applying the elementary row operation $R_2 := R_2 + 8R_1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058885/example-4726.json",
          "file_sha256": "254abb8fcfb98b74761f473b5021d021282a3977848566d42fdce2f0df1d571f"
        }
